{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4a9dc9fa-4e91-4159-a404-ce7f92513c2b","agentId":"aba1ccd874c146883","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Read two Bosch datasheets:\n(A) BME280: https://www.bosch-sensortec.com/media/boschsensortec/downloads/datasheets/bst-bme280-ds002.pdf\n(B) BMP280: https://www.bosch-sensortec.com/media/boschsensortec/downloads/datasheets/bst-bmp280-ds001.pdf\nReport ONLY these facts with exact numbers and section/table references:\nFrom (A) BME280:\n1. Register addresses: chip id (and value), reset, ctrl_hum, status (which bits mean measuring / im_update), ctrl_meas (bit fields osrs_t, osrs_p, mode and mode values), config, and the data registers press_msb..hum_lsb (addresses 0xF7–0xFE, and which bits of the xlsb registers are used).\n2. The note about ctrl_hum only taking effect after a write to ctrl_meas (exact wording).\n3. The calibration (trimming) parameter table: for every dig_T1..T3, dig_P1..P9, dig_H1..H6 give the register address(es) and data type (unsigned/signed short/char), including the exact bit packing of dig_H4 and dig_H5 across 0xE4/0xE5/0xE6.\n4. The integer compensation code from the datasheet section \"Compensation formulas\" for: temperature (BME280_compensate_T_int32), pressure 64-bit (BME280_compensate_P_int64) and humidity (bme280_compensate_H_int32). Quote the code EXACTLY, line by line, and the comments saying what units/format each returns (e.g. \"5123 equals 51.23 DegC\", Q24.8 pressure, Q22.10 humidity with their example values).\n5. In forced mode, the measurement time formula or typical/max measurement time for oversampling x1 on T, P, H.\nFrom (B) BMP280:\n6. The worked example table of the compensation (section \"Computation formula\" / example): all the dig_T/dig_P trimming values, adc_T, adc_P, and the resulting t_fine, temperature, and pressure values for the int32 and int64 versions. Quote every number exactly.\nIf something is not present, say so rather than guessing."},"uuid":"26fb6200-cc84-4dcc-a459-faecfdc9ac52","timestamp":"2026-10-28T20:42:00.310Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nicholasmarechal/Desktop/CS 370/Term Project","sessionId":"c86980ee-3397-43ca-bb7c-7a44e24e72ac","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"unified-frolicking-valiant"}
